	abstract = {Data structures are one of the fundamental concepts that a programmer must know. Many applications use one or other types of data structure. In this work, we developed a framework wherein, while playing game, data structure and algorithm (DSA) can be understood. It has many levels or rooms which are related to the concepts of data structures such as the linked list, trees, stacks, etc. The player has to use his/her knowledge in data structures and crack these levels. These levels are set in a way that the basic knowledge can be obtained through first few levels, while more knowledge and creativity is needed to clear final levels. The proposed work aims for making people get to know DSA concepts better, enjoy the process of learning, and a passion for computer science in a gamified manner. There is visualizers for each data structure needed for a level. So, a user can understand it better by learning visually and seeing how an operation takes place logically. This makes it easier for beginners to learn while more experienced programmers to practice their concepts. With few case studies, it is found that the learning pace is very high. While beginner’s pace of learning is much faster, the experienced learner’s pace is slightly slower. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2026.},
